    "created_at": "2026-06-08T07:11:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-06-08T07:11:30Z",
    "body": "Currently in Gecko, another case that's handled as \"not possible\" is if a node already has a parent when it's about to be inserted and detaching the node from the old parent immediately results in script attaching the node to something so that it has a parent again, the insertion is treated as \"not possible\". However, I'm not sure if it's actually possible (in the normal sense of the word) for a script to even run at that point.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
